INSERT INTO `documents` VALUES ('05bc7dd4c3b5c0dbd6d8ba14',2,'Juan Dela Cruz','Juan Dela Cruz','student','PRISM_ A Web-Based AI System for IERB Progress Monitoring and Automated Reporting.pdf','05bc7dd4c3b5c0dbd6d8ba14.pdf','application/pdf',1575203,'Research Protocol','Stage 1',1,1,NULL,'Research title: PRISM | Group: AMT-BSIT-Y4-2627-G01','Approved','the document has been approved, you may now submit','Claude Quiambao','2026-10-04 11:57:21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-04 11:53:30','2026-10-04 12:01:37','Juan Dela Cruz',0,NULL,NULL,NULL),('1caee15d57f3170b78e2e7f9',14,'NEIL PATRICK VILLANUEVA','NEIL PATRICK VILLANUEVA','student','Group-MTV-ACM.pdf','1caee15d57f3170b78e2e7f9.pdf','application/pdf',1058627,'Research Protocol','Completed',1,1,NULL,'Research title: Hierarchical Transformer Model | Group:  | Reviewer note: PLEASE','Approved','Good boss','Mads Admin','2026-10-09 22:11:28',NULL,NULL,'PurposeThis study develops a hierarchical transformer model for skeletal-based exercise recognition. It leverages MediaPipe for pose estimation and feature extraction, proposing a hierarchical attention mechanism that processes localized joint representations first before integrating them into a global representation. The approach aims to outperform non-hierarchical models and demonstrates practical applicability through a real-time exercise recognition framework.\n\nMajor points and methodology\nThe authors combine MediaPipe with a Transformer encoder featuring a hierarchical attention mechanism designed to capture spatial-temporal relationships. Key methodological choices include:\n- A two-stage attention process: initial local attention on individual joints followed by global attention across the body\n- Decoupling movement analysis for space (joint positions) and time (temporal dynamics) to reduce computational overhead\n- A buffered interval inference technique for real-time interval-based inference on live pose sequences with temporal smoothing for stability\n- Faster training times and reduced resource consumption compared to conventional approaches\n\nEthics and submission information\nNo ethics approval or institutional review board (IRB) documentation is included in the excerpt. The document contains no submission venue, publication details, or explicit disclosure of ethical considerations related to human subjects or data collection.\n\nAbsent or unclear information\n- Explicit ethics approval status is not stated\n- Submission location or publication venue is not specified beyond the abstract reference\n- Specific dataset details beyond NTU RGB+ D are not clearly enumerated\n- Implementation specifics, hyperparameters, and quantitative performance metrics are not visible in the excerpt\n- The full document coverage is noted as bounded, with portions omitted','2026-10-09 22:04:34','2026-10-09 22:12:21','NEIL PATRICK VILLANUEVA',0,NULL,NULL,NULL),('304ed681053e1e5d8c50f957',2,'Juan Dela Cruz','Juan Dela Cruz','student','QPF 042_Clean - Up Day Monitoring of Participation.pdf','304ed681053e1e5d8c50f957.pdf','application/pdf',158650,'Research Protocol','Stage 3',1,1,NULL,'Research title: PRISM | Group: AMT-BSIT-Y4-2627-G01 | Reviewer note: nothing','Submitted',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Purpose\nThis document is a Clean-Up Day Monitoring of Participation form from Centro Escolar University (Manila, Makati, Malolos). Its purpose is to record participation metrics during a clean-up day event through a structured table format.\n\nMajor points and methodology\nThe form contains three main sections: a title (\"Clean-Up Day Monitoring of Participation\"), a date field showing 9/1/2016, and two column headers—\"Quantity\" (for items like black bags) and \"Acknowledged by\" (for name and signature). The layout suggests a standard monitoring sheet where organizers would fill in quantities collected and have participants sign off on their acknowledgment. However, the document appears to be a template or partially completed form, as all data fields appear empty.\n\nEthics and submission information\nThe document includes a \"Copy to: Office Concerned\" directive referencing QPF 042 and indicates this is page 1 of 1. No ethical review board (IERB) approval information is visible in the excerpt. Submission procedures are not detailed beyond the copy-to instruction.\n\nAbsent or unclear information\n- Specific participation numbers are not recorded (quantity column is empty).\n- No participant names or signatures are present.\n- The exact clean-up day event details are missing.\n- Methodology for how participation was measured is not described beyond the form structure.\n- IERB approval status cannot be confirmed from this excerpt alone.','2026-10-09 13:52:15',NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),('5a582f8d7a1c4f3a9a8d3bbc',2,'Juan Dela Cruz','Juan Dela Cruz','student','CEU-IERB_SY26-27_1744_SciTech_Form12-Registration-and-Application-Form.docx','5a582f8d7a1c4f3a9a8d3bbc.docx','application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document',5208140,'Informed Consent Form','Stage 2',1,1,NULL,'Research title: PRISM | Group: AMT-BSIT-Y4-2627-G01','Approved','the document has been approved, proceed to submission','RPMS Administrator','2026-10-04 12:05:44',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-04 12:02:12','2026-10-08 19:15:17','Juan Dela Cruz',0,NULL,NULL,NULL),('91a8f2020e2ad2c6c201a1c0',13,'Cyrus Salvador','Cyrus Salvador','student','Screenshot 2025-05-24 104329.png','91a8f2020e2ad2c6c201a1c0.png','image/png',11869,'Research Protocol','Stage 1',1,1,NULL,'Research title: Lebron Suarez vs Lebron James | Group: NURSING-BSN-Y4-2627-G02 | Reviewer note: PLease SPeed NeeD tThis','Approved','nice one','Mads Admin','2026-10-09 16:04:16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-09 16:02:33','2026-10-09 16:05:31','Cyrus Salvador',0,NULL,NULL,NULL),('adbbd770dd4f5034169e6d96',4,'Sophia Yvonne L. Pateres','Sophia Yvonne L. Pateres','student','Informed Consent (English).pdf','adbbd770dd4f5034169e6d96.pdf','application/pdf',123351,'Informed Consent Form','Stage 1',1,1,NULL,'Research title: TEST | Group: AMT-BSA-Y4-2627-G01','Approved','','Claude Quiambao','2026-10-08 14:26:49',NULL,NULL,'Summary of Appendix E - Informed Consent Form\n\nPurpose\nThe study investigates how accounts payable management and budgeting practices relate to café profitability. Its aim is to determine how these financial management practices influence financial performance and to develop frameworks for optimizing financial planning and ensuring long-term sustainability in café businesses.\n\nMajor Points and Methodology\nParticipants will complete a survey questionnaire assessing their café\'s business profile and practices related to accounts payable management and budgeting, along with information relevant to profitability. Approximately twenty-two participants are expected. No invasive procedures, medical examinations, or treatments will be conducted. All information will be treated as confidential and used solely for academic research purposes, in accordance with the Data Privacy Act of 2012. Researchers will implement reasonable measures to protect personal information from unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or misuse. Data will be stored securely and accessible only to authorized personnel. After completion, participants may request general findings, though individual responses and personally identifiable information will remain confidential.\n\nEthics and Submission Information\nThe study is overseen by the CEU Institutional Ethics Review Board (CEU IERB). Participation is voluntary, and individuals may decline or withdraw at any time without penalty. The Principal Investigator and contact information are partially redacted. The study is subject to review and approval by the CEU IERB. Research data will be retained per institutional policies and securely disposed of after the required retention period. Post-study, participants may request general findings, but specific responses will not be disclosed.\n\nAbsent or Unclear Information\nKey identifiers are redacted: the principal investigator\'s name, department address, phone number, and contact person details are marked \"[identifier removed]\". The exact number of anticipated participants is approximate (22). While the study is noted as being subject to CEU IERB review and approval, the current document does not confirm final approval status. Specific data storage duration is described vaguely as \"required by applicable institutional research and data-protection policies\" without concrete timelines. The actual survey instrument is referenced but not included in the appendix.','2026-10-08 14:17:49',NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),('fbfd4e29787016fb2f0581fc',3,'Asha Ms. CEU Malolos','Asha Ms. CEU Malolos','student','20261004_114911.jpg','fbfd4e29787016fb2f0581fc.jpg','image/jpeg',2434349,'Research Protocol','Stage 1',1,1,NULL,'Research title: SYSTEMA | Group: AMT-BSIT-Y4-2627-G02','Denied','Bakit pusa???','RPMS Administrator','2026-10-05 10:26:32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-05 10:24:41',NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL);
